{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release lock-in final pass","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-006","severity":"medium","summary":"The spec says a loop message at command completion loses only model reasoning because “no command is in flight.” The implementation does not establish that invariant: another command may still be running, and the completion-triggered action kills the executor process group. A consumer could underestimate interruption and partial-effect risk.","evidence":["Spec: “At a command completion (loop messages), no command is in flight, so only the model's in-progress reasoning is lost.”","`_Timeline.in_flight()` tracks all started, unfinished commands; `_on_complete()` schedules loop actions without checking that the other commands have finished.","`LaneProgressWatch.observe_event()` applies the action, whose kill callback stops the process group. The release notes also say a loop message does not wait for a running command."],"action":"Qualify the spec to account for another command still running and possible partial effects, or establish serial command execution before claiming only reasoning is lost."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"R-003 timing claim","bin":"fixed","disposition":"The spec now calls windows nominal, disclaims a hard wall-clock bound, and gives only due-check counts; no closed-form bound is needed."},{"concern":"R-004 request-delivery and stop sequence","bin":"fixed","disposition":"The guide describes request delivery followed by a later empty check stopping the lane, with a young-command delay."},{"concern":"R-005 young-command exception in guide and ProgressRule docstring","bin":"fixed","disposition":"Both now state that a young command can delay either request delivery or stopping by a check."},{"concern":"Progress rule can be disabled with a zero window","bin":"advisory","disposition":"The release notes and spec state the zero-value opt-out; the guide's short summary does not create a material consumer error in this review."}],"next_move":"Resolve R-006 before release lock-in; R-003 and R-004 are fixed in the reviewed input.","non_claims":["Reviewed the 17 identity-bound inline files only; did not inspect workspace paths, run tests, or verify live executor behavior."]}
